	regionKind = "zone",
	kind = "region",
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Loch Modan is a broad basin of hills and pine woods in Khaz Modan, east of {link:dun-morogh}Dun Morogh{/link}. At its heart lies {link:the-loch}the Loch{/link}, the great lake that gives the land its name, held back at its northern end by the {link:stonewrought-dam}Stonewrought Dam{/link}. The town of {link:thelsamar}Thelsamar{/link} stands near its western shore. Dwarven towers keep the passes that run west to {link:ironforge}Ironforge{/link}, north to the {link:wetlands}Wetlands{/link} and south toward the {link:searing-gorge}Searing Gorge{/link}. It is a gentler country than the snows of Dun Morogh, rich in ore, game and fish, and the {link:dwarves}dwarves{/link} of the {link:kingdom-of-ironforge}Kingdom of Ironforge{/link} have long held it as their own.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[No chronicle records when the dwarves first settled the shores of {link:the-loch}the Loch{/link}, or when the {link:stonewrought-dam}Stonewrought Dam{/link} was raised. The land is old in their history. In the {link:valley-of-kings}Valley of Kings{/link}, two great statues stand guard over the southern road. They honor Madoran Bronzebeard and Khardros Wildhammer, who led their clans in the age of the War of the Three Hammers. It is told that their sons raised the statues after that war to watch over the road to the south, as a warning to any who would march on the dwarven realms again.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Present Day",
			text = [=[Loch Modan is a land under siege, and its defenders are few. The {link:ironforge}Ironforge{/link} Reserve has been called away to fight for the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link} on distant fronts, and the reinforcements promised to {link:the-loch}the Loch{/link} have never come. {link:captain-rugelfuss}Captain Rugelfuss{/link} holds the {link:valley-of-kings}Valley of Kings{/link} with a single regiment, while the {link:troggs}troggs{/link} of the {link:stonesplinter-troggs}Stonesplinter tribe{/link} boil out of the southern hills and overrun the Explorers' dig beside the lake. {link:ogres}Ogres{/link} of the {link:mo-grosh-ogres}Mo'grosh clan{/link} raid from the north-east. {link:kobolds}Kobolds{/link} have taken the {link:silver-stream-mine}Silver Stream Mine{/link}. Worst of all, {link:dark-iron-dwarves}Dark Iron{/link} saboteurs have crept up to the dam itself, and they have friends among those the dwarves trust. In {link:thelsamar}Thelsamar{/link}, {link:magistrate-bluntnose}Magistrate Bluntnose{/link} has been told that he must wait months for a handful of soldiers. He has stopped waiting, and he pays in good coin any stranger who will fight.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Inhabitants",
			text = [=[• {b}The dwarves of {link:ironforge}Ironforge{/link}.{/b} Mountaineers, miners, fishers and cooks live in {link:thelsamar}Thelsamar{/link} and man the towers along the passes.
• {b}The Explorers' League.{/b} From its branch in Thelsamar, the {link:explorers-league}Explorers' League{/link} supplies {link:prospector-ironband}Prospector Ironband{/link}'s dig among the ruins east of the lake.
• {b}The hunters of the {link:the-farstrider-lodge}Farstrider Lodge{/link}.{/b} {link:dwarves}Dwarves{/link}, humans and a {link:high-elves}high elf{/link} keep a hunting lodge in the eastern hills.
• {b}The {link:stonesplinter-troggs}Stonesplinter troggs{/link}.{/b} They hold the southern valleys, the islands of {link:the-loch}the Loch{/link} and the ruins of the excavation.
• {b}The {link:mo-grosh-ogres}Mo'grosh ogres{/link}.{/b} A clan of {link:ogres}ogres{/link} has made its stronghold in the caves of the north-east.
• {b}The {link:tunnel-rat-kobolds}Tunnel Rat kobolds{/link}.{/b} {link:kobolds}Kobolds{/link} have dug dens in the western foothills and filled the {link:silver-stream-mine}Silver Stream Mine{/link}.
• {b}The {link:dark-iron-dwarves}Dark Irons{/link}.{/b} Sappers and insurgents lurk about the dam, and at least one of their agents hid among the dwarves' own porters.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The Three Hammers.{/b} After the war of the three clans, the kings of the Bronzebeards and the Wildhammers were remembered in stone at the southern gate of {link:the-loch}the Loch{/link}.
• {b}The Second War.{/b} When the {link:horde}Horde{/link} overran Khaz Modan in the {link:second-war}Second War{/link}, the loch country fell under orcish rule. The dwarves won it back, but the wrecks of orcish catapults and wagons still lie in the shallows and behind the old silver mine.
• {b}The Excavation.{/b} The {link:explorers-league}Explorers' League{/link} opened a dig among ancient ruins south-east of the Loch. Its diggers found strange carved idols, and soon after, the troggs came up out of the ground.
• {b}The Present Day.{/b} Now the Loch is guarded by the few who stayed behind, and by whatever help they can hire.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Lore of the Loch",
			text = [=[• {link:thelsamar}Thelsamar{/link} is famous for its blood sausages: bear meat, stuffed into boar casings and spiced with the ichor of spiders. The cook insists that it is harder than it looks.
• The crocolisks of {link:the-loch}the Loch{/link} are prized for their skins and their meat, but they have dug in on the lake's islands, and few hunters bring them down without a scar.
• The mountaineers of the Loch drink Shimmer Stout, brewed in far {link:brewnall-village}Brewnall Village{/link}. One who tasted it swore that it made his limbs so light he felt he could fly.
• Snow lies in {link:south-gate-pass}South Gate Pass{/link} the whole year round, though the shores of the Loch below are green.]=],
		},
	},
})

